ogle Docs, Google Sheets, and Google Slides through one unified Google Drive plugin. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/google-drive/fef63ecf/skills/google-drive/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive-comments: Write, reply to, and resolve Google Drive comments on Docs, Sheets, Slides, and Drive files with evidence-backed location context. Use when the user asks to leave comments, review a file with comments, respond to comment threads, or resolve Drive comments. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/google-drive/fef63ecf/skills/google-drive-comments/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-sheets: Analyze and edit connected Google Sheets with range precision. Use when the user wants to create Google Sheets, find a spreadsheet, inspect tabs or ranges, search rows, plan formulas, create or repair charts, clean or restructure tables, write concise summaries, or make explicit cell-range updates. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/google-drive/fef63ecf/skills/google-sheets/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-slides: Google Slides work for finding, reading, summarizing, creating, importing, visual cleanup, template migration, structural repair, and content edits in native Slides decks. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/google-drive/fef63ecf/skills/google-slides/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order: Generate a textbook-style stroke-order diagram (SVG) for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke showing completed strokes in black, the current stroke highlighted with a red number and directional arrow at its starting point, and remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill whenever the user asks how to write a Japanese character, requests stroke order, asks \"in what order do I draw X\", wants to learn or memorize a kanji, asks to decompose a character into strokes, says \"show me the strokes for X\", mentions 書き順 / kakijun, or shows a stroke-order ch